# Summary

1. δ/δJ inserts a field.

2. Translation of a dummy φ produces Schwinger–Dyson equations.

3. A symmetry of S and of Dφ produces Ward identities.

4. Gauge fixing is the Jacobian when the naive measure is not invariant.

5. None of this replaces regularization or a complete set of diagrams.

